#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:46
msgid ""
":ref:`CanvasModulate<class_CanvasModulate>` is used to darken the scene."
msgstr ""
"El :ref:`CanvasModulate<class_CanvasModulate>` es usado para oscurecer la "
"escena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:48
msgid ""
":ref:`Sprites <class_Sprite>` are used to display the textures for the light "
"blobs, the background, and for the shadow casters."
msgstr ""
"Los :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` son usados para mostrar las texturas de los "
"puntos de luz, el fondo y los generadores de sombra."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:51
msgid ""
":ref:`Light2Ds <class_Light2D>` are used to light the scene. The way a light "
"typically works is by adding a selected texture over the rest of the scene "
"to simulate lighting. But it can be used in other ways, for example masking "
"out parts of the scene."
msgstr ""
"Los :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>` son usados para iluminar la escena. El "
"modo en que una luz trabaja es sumando la textura seleccionada al resto de "
"la escena para simular la iluminación. Pero puede ser usada de otros modos, "
"por ejemplo como máscaras para ocultar parte de la escena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:55
msgid ""
":ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>` are used to tell the shader "
"which parts of the scene cast shadows. The shadows appear only on areas "
"covered by the :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>` and their direction is based "
"on the center of the :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`."
msgstr ""
"Los :ref:`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>` se utilizan para decirle "
"al shader qué parte de la escena debe producir sombra. La sombra aparece "
"sólo en areas cubiertas por el :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>` y su dirección "
"está basada en el centro del :ref:`Light2D <class_Light2D>`."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:60
#: tutorials/3d/introduction_to_3d.rst:218
#: tutorials/performance/batching.rst:149
msgid "Lights"
msgstr "Luces"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:62
msgid ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` cover the entire extent of their respective "
"Texture. They use additive blending to add the color of their texture to the "
"scene."
msgstr ""
"Los :ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` cubren la total extensión de la textura "
"correspondiente. Usan mezcla aditiva para agregar color de su textura a la "
"escena."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:67
msgid ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` have four ``Modes``: ``Add``, ``Sub``, "
"``Mix``, and ``Mask``."
msgstr ""
":ref:`Lights <class_Light2D>` Tiene 4 modos en la propiedad ``Mode``: "
"``Add``, ``Sub``, ``Mix``, and ``Mask``."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:69
msgid ""
"``Add`` adds the color of the light texture to the scene. It brightens the "
"area under the light."
msgstr ""
"``Add`` suma el color de la textura de la luz a la escena. Esto ilumina el "
"área bajo la luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:71
msgid ""
"``Sub`` subtracts the color of the light from the scene. It darkens the area "
"under the light."
msgstr ""
"``Sub`` resta el color de la luz en la escena. Esto oscurece el área bajo la "
"luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:73
msgid ""
"``Mix`` mixes the color of the light with the underlying scene. The "
"resulting brightness is halfway between the color of the light and the color "
"underneath."
msgstr ""
"``Mix`` mezcla el color de la luz con la escena cubierta. Esto resulta en "
"una iluminación que está entre el color de la luz y el de la escena que se "
"encuentra debajo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:76
msgid ""
"``Mask`` is used to mask out areas that are covered by the light. Masked out "
"areas are hidden or revealed based on the color of the light."
msgstr ""
"``Mask`` es usada para enmascarar áreas que están cubiertas por la luz. Las "
"áreas enmascaradas serán ocultadas o reveladas basado en el color de la luz."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:79
msgid ""
"For the demo the lights have two components, the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` itself (which is the effect of the light), and a :ref:"
"`Sprite <class_Sprite>` blob which is an image showing the location of the "
"light source. A child :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` is not necessary to make "
"a :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` work."
msgstr ""
"Para la demostración, las luces tienen dos componentes, la :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` (luz) que representa el efecto de iluminación, y un :ref:"
"`Sprite <class_Sprite>` que es una imagen que muestra el origen de la luz. "
"Un hijo :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` no es necesario para que un nodo :ref:"
"`Light2D <class_Light2D>` funcione."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:87
msgid "Shadows"
msgstr "Sombras"

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:89
msgid ""
"Shadows are made by intersecting a :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` with a :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`."
msgstr ""
"Las sombras se hacen mediante una intersección de un :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` con un :ref:`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>`."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:91
msgid ""
"By default shadows are turned off. To turn them on click on the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` and under the Shadows section check ``Enabled``."
msgstr ""
"Por defecto, las sombras están apagadas. Para encenderlas debes hacer clic "
"en el nodo :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` y en la sección Shadows marcar "
"``Enabled``."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:94
msgid ""
"In the demo we are using a :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` with a Texture on it "
"to make the \"Shadow Casters\", but in reality all you need is a couple of :"
"ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>`. By itself the :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>` looks like a dark spot and in this "
"demo the :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` is just a black square."
msgstr ""
"En la demo se usa un :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` con una textura para hacer "
"los \"generadores de sombra\" pero, en realidad, todo lo que necesitas es "
"unos cuantos nodos :ref:`LightOccluder2Ds <class_LightOccluder2D>`. Por sí "
"mismo, el :ref:`LightOccluder2D <class_LightOccluder2D>` se ve como un punto "
"oscuro y en la demo, el :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` es sólo un cuadrado "
"negro."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:102
msgid ""
"Now that we have covered the basics of the nodes being used, we can now walk "
"step by step through the process of making a scene like the one found in the "
"demo."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que hemos cubierto lo básico de los nodos que usaremos, podemos ir "
"paso a paso en el proceso de hacer una escena como la de la demo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:105
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First add a :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` and set its texture to the "
"background image. For your game this can be any background you choose. For "
"this style of shadow it is most likely to be a floor texture."
msgstr ""
"Primero agrega un :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` y asigna su textura a "
"`background image <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-demo-"
"projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/background.png>`_. Para tu juego, esto "
"puede ser cualquier otra imagen de fondo. Para este estilo de sombra sería "
"algo como una textura de piso."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:111
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next create three :ref:`Light2D's <class_Light2D>` and set their textures to "
"the light image. You can alter their color in the top section. By default "
"shadows are turned off and the ``mode`` is set to ``add``. This means that "
"each light adds its own color to whatever is underneath."
msgstr ""
"Luego crea tres :ref:`Light2D's <class_Light2D>` y asigna en sus texturas a "
"`light image <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-demo-"
"projects/master/2d/lights_and_shadows/light.png>`_. Puedes alterar el color "
"en la sección superior. Por defecto las sombras están apagadas y el ``mode`` "
"en tipo ``add``. Lo que significa que cada luz agrega su propio color a lo "
"que esté al fondo."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:118
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next add a child :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` to each of the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` nodes, and set the :ref:`Sprite's <class_Sprite>` texture "
"to the blob image. Each of these should stay centered on the :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` node. The blob is the image of the light itself while the :"
"ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` shows the effect that the light has on the "
"scene. The :ref:`LightOccluder2D's <class_LightOccluder2D>` will treat the "
"position of the light as the center of the :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>` "
"node, which is why we want the blob to be centered on its parent :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>`."
msgstr ""
"Como paso siguiente agregaremos un hijo :ref:`Sprite <class_Sprite>` a cada "
"nodo :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`, y asignaremos en su textura la `blob "
"image <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/"
"master/2d/lights_and_shadows/spot.png>`_. Cada uno de esos deberá estar "
"centrados en el nodo :ref:`Light <class_Light2D> correspondiente. Esta "
"imagen es la imagen que representa al emisor de luz mientras que :ref:`Light "
"<class_Light2D>` muestra el efecto de la luz sobre la escena. El :ref:"
"`LightOccluder2D's <class_LightOccluder2D>` tomará como centro de la luz a "
"la posición del nodo :ref:`Light <class_Light2D>`, es por eso que queremos "
"que el Sprite esté centrado en el padre."

#: tutorials/2d/2d_lights_and_shadows.rst:127
